From 383fd20ccd9fe670e0fcb5af08c613859e1b9e3f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: noon-at-cgn <75719527+noon-at-cgn@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 31 Oct 2026 23:39:56 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 29/53] Backport vllm-project/vllm#62113: 16-byte-align
 per-token-head KV slots so Triton vectorizes loads

[Perf][Attention] TRITON_ATTN packs per-token-head int8/fp8 KV as
[K | k_scale | V | v_scale]; customize_spec now pads each K/V half to 16 bytes
(head_size 256 int8: 520 -> 544 B per slot, V at +272; 128: 264 -> 288).
INT4 stays unpadded. _ensure_scale_caches takes the head size from the impl
instead of inferring it from the content width.

Open upstream (vllm-project/vllm#62113, head 9c3f9f8798bc, needs-rebase);
retire this pick when upstream merges. Applied by hand (the upstream diff does
not apply to this base). Dropped: the .buildkite/intel_jobs deselect (file not
in this tree) and the test's split-K parametrization (needs upstream's
_spy_reduce_segments helper, not in this base). Kept: the backend
read-through in test_per_token_kv_cache and the parametrized
test_unpadded_page_size_includes_per_token_head_scales.
